.TH HOSTS-LINT 1 "October 2026" "SASD Freeware" "User Commands"
.SH NAME
hosts-lint \- perform basic syntax checks on a hosts file
.SH SYNOPSIS
.B hosts-lint
.RB [ --file " PATH]"
.SH DESCRIPTION
Checks IPv4 and IPv6 addresses, hostnames, and aliases in a hosts(5)
style file without modifying it. Prints counts of parsed entries,
unique names, warnings and errors. Conflicting address mappings for
the same name are reported as warnings and may be intentional.
.SH OPTIONS
.TP
.BI --file " PATH"
Input path (default /etc/hosts).
.TP
.BR -h , " --help"
Show usage.
.SH EXIT STATUS
0 for successful syntax validation (including warnings),
1 for malformed entries, 2 for incorrect usage, and nonzero on I/O failures.
.SH EXAMPLE
.B hosts-lint --file ./hosts.candidate
.SH NOTES
Not a DNS query tool or a full parser for platform-specific extensions.
.SH SEE ALSO
.BR hosts (5)
